"donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":0.0889559,"donor_lfcse":0.0973583,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":9.78658e-06,"degas_log2fc":-0.277697,"degas_padj":1.0738e-07},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"RNF11","gene_symbol_current":"RNF11","gene_id":"ENSG00000123091","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.00105015,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0841383,"nucleus_score":3.41963,"pct_ad":0.240359,"pct_control":0.230021,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.767138,"donor_log2fc":0.0907657,"donor_lfcse":0.0661843,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0216054,"degas_log2fc":-0.186047,"degas_padj":2.23656e-14}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000123091","module":"blue","kme":0.0361111,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.506562,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000123091","module":"red","kme":0.293318,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.0519952,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_id":"ENSG00000123091","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0479816,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.398013,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000123091","entrez_id":["26994"],"uniprot":["Q9Y3C5"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene contains a RING-H2 finger motif, which is known to be important for protein-protein interactions. The expression of this gene has been shown to be induced by mutant RET proteins (MEN2A/MEN2B). The germline mutations in RET gene are known to be responsible for the development of multiple endocrine neoplasia (MEN). [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9Y3C5","text":"Essential component of a ubiquitin-editing protein complex, comprising also TNFAIP3, ITCH and TAX1BP1, that ensures the transient nature of inflammatory signaling pathways. Promotes the association of TNFAIP3 to RIPK1 after TNF stimulation. TNFAIP3 deubiquitinates 'Lys-63' polyubiquitin chains on RIPK1 and catalyzes the formation of 'Lys-48'-polyubiquitin chains. This leads to RIPK1 proteasomal degradation and consequently termination of the TNF- or LPS-mediated activation of NF-kappa-B. Recruits STAMBP to the E3 ubiquitin-ligase SMURF2 for ubiquitination, leading to its degradation by the 26S proteasome."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}